      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While protecting human rights is noble, the moral cost of preemptive intervention is too high because it inevitably leads to unintended consequences like regime collapse, civil war, and the very authoritarianism we sought to prevent. A stronger moral framework requires that we only intervene when there is an imminent, specific threat to our own citizens, not to abstract future atrocities in distant lands. We must avoid the trap of believing our military can solve complex political problems or that we have the right to dictate the future of sovereign nations.",
