    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds like a very convenient way to avoid making hard choices. You're basically saying that human rights are secondary to legalistic concepts like sovereignty. Isn't that a bit of a hollow stance when you're talking about real people suffering? If we know a genocide is coming and we do nothing because of \"sovereignty,\" aren't we just being morally cowardly?",
